      "Turn-flow example: 1. **The Pitch**: The player to the dealer's left (the Pitcher) leads any card. The suit of this card immediately becomes trumps for the hand. 2. **Trick Play**: Follow suit if possible. You may trump instead of following suit, even if you hold a card of the led suit. 3. **The 'Low' Hunt**: Unlike other variants, the 'Low' point is awarded to the team that WINS the trick containing the lowest trump card that was dealt in that hand. 4. **Scoring Order**: Points are counted and pegged in the following order: High, Low, Jack, Game.",
      'Scoring example: Pegging points immediately at the end of the hand. First team to reach 11 points wins. The scoring order (H-L-J-G) is critical if both teams cross the 11-point threshold in the same deal..',
